Subject: [PATCH] platform-mc: Add state sensor support as per DSP0248

Add support for PLDM state sensors in the platform-mc component,
extending the existing numeric sensor capabilities. This
implementation is in compliance with DMTF PLDM specification
DSP0248.

Changes include:
- Add StateSensor class (state_sensor.cpp/hpp) to handle state
  sensor reading updates and export status to D-Bus interfaces
  according to DSP0248 specification
- Parse and store PLDM_STATE_SENSOR_PDR records during terminus
  PDR initialization
- Create D-Bus interfaces for availability, operational status,
  and associations

The StateSensor implementation follows the same pattern as
NumericSensor with D-Bus interface creation, sensor reading
updates, and error handling.

Implementation of PLDM State Set specification DSP0249 to
support this will be done part of different commit. This
commit covers the base state sensors as per base spec DSP0248.

Tested: Tested on Alon8 platform with CoonectX devices and
all state sensors successfully created and exposed on D-Bus.
```
    | |- /xyz/openbmc_project/sensors/state
    | | |- /xyz/openbmc_project/sensors/state/Terminus_18_Sensor_200
    | | |- /xyz/openbmc_project/sensors/state/Terminus_18_Sensor_201
    | | |- /xyz/openbmc_project/sensors/state/Terminus_18_Sensor_5
    | | |- /xyz/openbmc_project/sensors/state/Terminus_18_Sensor_60
```

